{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/822930-mercy-thompson-world-campaign","id":822930,"title":"Mercy Thompson world campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-03T18:10:44-08:00","id":822930,"title":"Mercy Thompson world campaign","content":"I don't know how many of you have read Patricia Briggs'<i> Mercy Thompson</i> series, but in short it's about a coyote shifter among a pack of werewolves... It ends up spanning a large part of the northwestern U.S., and includes myths and tales from all through the world's history.<br /> <br /> My group is planning a campaign set in this world, in which werewolves, fae, and witches are all not only real, but out and known by mankind. In addition vampires and other gods are real, but not &quot;out&quot; to mankind.<br /> <br /> Additionally, native american scions (who my players will all be making characters of) are all born with the additional ability of a mundane form of their divine parent's animal form.<br /> <br /> <b>spoiler alert: </b>Just as Mercy is a child of Coyote, and so can become a coyote, children of raven, owl, bear, bobcat, wolf, etc will gain the shape of their parent.<br /> <br /> I'm excited by this idea, and figured I'd share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10163-toomuchjesus","name":"Toomuchjesus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T23:50:26-08:00","id":826610,"title":"","content":"I love this. I read that series AGES ago but never finished, I'll have to see how it holds up now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1012-sorcerymon","name":"Sorcerymon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1012_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:12:46-08:00","id":827082,"title":"","content":"I really enjoy the series, but I can't help thinking Scion is one of the <i>worst</i> systems for that world. You need a system that handles all sorts of supernatural creatures very flexibly. Scion is <b>not</b> that system. I'd honestly suggest giving something like Unknown Armies, Witchcraft, D6 Modern, D20 Modern, Urban Arcana, or Savage Worlds a try. Savage Worlds is a <i>really</i> good system and handles all kinds of powers very, very well. <br /> <br /> While Mercy <b>is</b> a &quot;scion&quot; of Coyote... she isn't <i>anything</i> near the level of even a Hero Scion. She has no Epic Attributes, no Purviews. <i>Maybe</i> a few Knacks, but mostly she has a very few, very specific, very unique abilities that Scion really doesn't have <i>any</i> way to represent at low-Legend scales. Scion just isn't very <i>good</i> at doing modern urban fantasy. That isn't what it's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:58:47-08:00","id":827258,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd use GURPS, which handles &quot;street-level&quot; urban fantasy stuff prety well. I've already run a successful &quot;World of Darkness - Hunters&quot; campaign using it. It's more work as GM at first, but it is perfect for Mercy Thompson-type stuff perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:23:10-08:00","id":827403,"title":"","content":"Hopefully, <i>Scion: Origins</i> will have systems which make it easier to run more urban fantasy style games. In any case, it sounds like a concept you could have a lot of fun with. Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}